id: pm-beads-080q
title: beads validate and beads diff fail to register on pm-cli 2026.7.27 because each redeclares the host-owned --json global
description: "pm-cli 2026.7.27 (GH-719) makes the host reject any extension command whose flags shadow a host-owned global flag. beads validate and beads diff both declared { long: \"--json\" } in their flags arrays (VALIDATE_FLAGS and DIFF_FLAGS), so both commands failed to register against a real pm host. The suite never caught this because every smoke test built a hand-rolled api double that accepts all registrations unconditionally. Additionally, the audit:prod script used a bare 'npm audit --omit=dev' that fails with EALLOWSCRIPTS in project-scoped installs. Fix: drop both --json flag declarations, read the value from ctx.global.json in parseDiffOptions and the validate handler, rebuild the smoke suite on the SDK createExtensionTestHarness so pm's real activation engine validates registration, add a suite-wide guard, and fix audit:prod to strip npm_config_allow_scripts."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T05:14:42.040Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T05:14:46.623Z"
author: pi-agent
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T05:14:46.623Z",pi-agent,"Verified end-to-end: activation probe prints failed=[]; full suite 85/85 pass; release:check green. Also fixed pre-existing audit:prod EALLOWSCRIPTS bug."
body: ""
